From 5f4aeb015fffd1affaba3915ec5892c422f144b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Yin <peter.yin@quantatw.com>
Date: Tue, 31 Mar 2026 20:37:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] terminus: replace inventory and sensor configuration

Some devices (e.g. OCP NIC) do not provide auxiliary sensor names.
When auxiliary names are unavailable, pldmd uses a combination of
terminus ID and sensor ID as the sensor name.

Introduce fetchEntityManagerConfiguration to query EntityManager via
GetManagedObjects using the associated inventory path. This allows
pldmd to discover PLDM sensor mappings and update auxiliary sensor
names based on sensor ID and Name properties.

EM link:https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/86156

Testing:
On the Harma platform, replace the default PLDM sensor and inventory
names with platform-specific names.

Sensor name updates:
- Terminus_1_Sensor_300 to NIC_TEMPERATURE1
- Terminus_1_Sensor_500 to NIC_TEMPERATURE2

Inventory name update:
- MINERVA_AEGIS to Minerva_Aegis

Change-Id: I326459c75d6dc8b822302eaf7f0b85f13412b0db
Signed-off-by: Peter Yin <peter.yin@quantatw.com>
